[[:db/retract 17592186162571 :question/answer-fields 17592186160718] {:db/id 17592186162571 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 10 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 8 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -14 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary row operations \n\n- ${R}_{2}:=…$\n- ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$\n- ${R}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries below ${a}_{11}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 10 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 8 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 8 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -14 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-db7b0ab2-ace0-5e5f-813e-a09b5ee8870d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-db7b0ab2-ace0-5e5f-813e-a09b5ee8870d" :answer-field/id #uuid "db7b0ab2-ace0-5e5f-813e-a09b5ee8870d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-39feaea9-f53d-5ee3-a622-cbfc2b43387f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-caaba1b9-461d-5d04-a1fd-8f442d709eb4" "answer-c49a7ab3-b457-50a7-8db3-96d09691584e" "answer-39feaea9-f53d-5ee3-a622-cbfc2b43387f" "answer-a66beb93-cf63-56e5-af86-8bf4482be7a2" "answer-3b22a6a4-61fa-5183-9649-c580b3bc7020"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caaba1b9-461d-5d04-a1fd-8f442d709eb4" :answer/id #uuid "caaba1b9-461d-5d04-a1fd-8f442d709eb4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c49a7ab3-b457-50a7-8db3-96d09691584e" :answer/id #uuid "c49a7ab3-b457-50a7-8db3-96d09691584e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-2{R}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39feaea9-f53d-5ee3-a622-cbfc2b43387f" :answer/id #uuid "39feaea9-f53d-5ee3-a622-cbfc2b43387f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a66beb93-cf63-56e5-af86-8bf4482be7a2" :answer/id #uuid "a66beb93-cf63-56e5-af86-8bf4482be7a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b22a6a4-61fa-5183-9649-c580b3bc7020" :answer/id #uuid "3b22a6a4-61fa-5183-9649-c580b3bc7020" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-2{R}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161968 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e8820685-174a-5aac-b0a4-a6b54f80941e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e8820685-174a-5aac-b0a4-a6b54f80941e" :question/id #uuid "e8820685-174a-5aac-b0a4-a6b54f80941e" :question/math-academy-id "q-91188" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of ${a}_{31}=3$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3ff26ed5-7a58-584f-95b3-0a0e85d61774"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3ff26ed5-7a58-584f-95b3-0a0e85d61774" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ff26ed5-7a58-584f-95b3-0a0e85d61774" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-aa1f46ac-844a-5bb2-b9b6-04cb4156fcf9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-99b872c0-2012-5d57-9afd-16e6b6bde53b" "answer-4c552dee-9870-5f80-99c4-13a42caad182" "answer-166feab7-a264-55aa-acc5-4218b97966a9" "answer-aa1f46ac-844a-5bb2-b9b6-04cb4156fcf9" "answer-a66ce929-c767-5507-b64f-0b3826324583"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99b872c0-2012-5d57-9afd-16e6b6bde53b" :answer/id #uuid "99b872c0-2012-5d57-9afd-16e6b6bde53b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c552dee-9870-5f80-99c4-13a42caad182" :answer/id #uuid "4c552dee-9870-5f80-99c4-13a42caad182" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+3{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+2{C}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-166feab7-a264-55aa-acc5-4218b97966a9" :answer/id #uuid "166feab7-a264-55aa-acc5-4218b97966a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa1f46ac-844a-5bb2-b9b6-04cb4156fcf9" :answer/id #uuid "aa1f46ac-844a-5bb2-b9b6-04cb4156fcf9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a66ce929-c767-5507-b64f-0b3826324583" :answer/id #uuid "a66ce929-c767-5507-b64f-0b3826324583" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-2{C}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-61c7230c-4be1-54c6-95c3-76fe59986f88" :activity/id #uuid "61c7230c-4be1-54c6-95c3-76fe59986f88" :activity/title "Creating Rows or Columns Containing Zeros Using Gaussian Elimination" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050527 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-3be10ce9-b323-5320-8a6b-fd2980284abe" "step-481012f0-867f-5ff8-ba1d-2515c1153226" "step-9cc0e464-95dc-5890-bc99-303c34184e49"] :activity/first-step "step-3be10ce9-b323-5320-8a6b-fd2980284abe" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-3be10ce9-b323-5320-8a6b-fd2980284abe" :step/id #uuid "3be10ce9-b323-5320-8a6b-fd2980284abe" :step/content 17592186329695 :step/next "step-481012f0-867f-5ff8-ba1d-2515c1153226" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-481012f0-867f-5ff8-ba1d-2515c1153226" :step/id #uuid "481012f0-867f-5ff8-ba1d-2515c1153226" :step/content 17592186162571 :step/next "step-9cc0e464-95dc-5890-bc99-303c34184e4